# Experiment Log

## Date: 2026-05-15 (Friday)
## Topic
MC-G105 denoise pipeline review, denoise-priority v2 redesign, and new Phase 1 training start.

## Summary
Today focused on validating whether the current public-HR synthetic degradation pipeline is producing a useful denoise learning signal for `SVFocusDenoiseNet` dim32/block2. Visual comparison showed that the 260514 Phase 1 and Phase 2 outputs were almost identical, and Phase 2 did not visibly improve the foliage/shadow noise that the deploy model suppresses. The project constraint was clarified: the operating student model remains `SVFocusDenoiseNet` dim32/block2, with MTKD planned later; the immediate goal is to make the synthetic degradation pipeline itself teach the small model to remove 2D/3D-like noise, hot pixels, and chroma noise while reducing deploy-style text blur.

